window.MONSTER_CHUNK_151 = [{"name":"Lilith (Former Queen of Hell)","cr":16,"xp":76800,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect magic"}],"auras":["fear (20 ft., Will DC 29)"],"ac":33,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +9 natural, +11 profane","hp":178,"hd":"17d10+85","hdvalue":17,"hp_mods":["regeneration 10 (good, silver)"],"fort":10,"ref":13,"will":16,"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":27,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"+2 axiomatic unholy longsword +25 (1d8+7/19-20) or 2 claws +22 (1d6+5)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"},{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"greater dispel magic"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"mass hold monster"},{"spell":"see invisibility"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"lightning bolt"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 8, 2d4 erinyes, 1d6 lilins, or 1d4 barbed devils 100% or 1 pit fiend 40%"},{"spell":"unholy blight"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]},{"frequency":"1/week","spells":[{"spell":"wish"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":16,"constitution":21,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":19,"charisma":33,"baseatk":17,"cmb":22,"cmd":46,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (fireball)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (longsword)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":23},{"skill":"Bluff","value":35},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":32},{"skill":"Disguise","value":35},{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":35},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":28}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Infernal","Terran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Infernus)"],"organizations":["solitary","entourage (Lilith plus 2-4 erinyes or lilins)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"A curvaceous and beautiful woman with cinnamon-brown skin, dark red hair, and shining emerald eyes stands before you. She is scantily clad in scarlet robes and carries a longsword at her side.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fear Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by her fear aura for one day. Other devils are immune to the aura. The save DC is Charisma-based. Amaheuris: Lilith carries a unique +2 axiomatic unholy longsword. Once per day, she can fire a finger of death (caster level 15th) from her weapon at a single target she can see and that is within 50 ft. A target struck must succeed on a DC 20 Fortitude save or die. Even if the save succeeds, the target takes 3d6+10 points of damage."}],"description":"Lilith was once consort to Moloch, ruler of the 6th plane of Hell. When the Great Uprising that pitted Lucifer and his minions against Asmodeus and his minions occurred, Lilith sided with Lucifer. When Moloch heard of her betrayal he raged against her, nearly killing her. If not for the swift action of several of her lilins (who sacrificed themselves for her), she would have surely been killed. During the commotion and chaos, she was spirited away to a safe location by Xaphan.\n\nWhen Lucifer constructed the plane of Infernus, Lilith had found her new home. She became a member of Lucifer's court and serves as one of his concubines and chief officers (ruling and commanding several companies of lilins). Lucifer, as of late has taken a special interest in her and rumors abound that should he take a queen to rule beside him it will be Lilith. This has infuriated more than one of his consorts, especially Demoriel who jealously wants the throne of Infernus and Lucifer all to herself. Lilith knows of Demoriel's jealousy and always keeps an open eye on her (including planting several spies in Demoriel's camp).\n\nLilith appears as an insanely comely female standing 5'7\" tall and weighing roughly 130 pounds. Her skin is cinnamon colored and her hair, waist length and blood red. Her eyes are emerald green and sparkle under the fiery skies of Infernus. Her hands end in claws and underneath her thick hair she hides two tiny dark black horns. She has a small pair of leathery black bat-like wings that she can fold against her back and hide under her robes at a moment's notice should the need for such deception arise.\n\n\"…and thus, Lucifer created Infernus, a plane of eternal and everlasting fire and suffering: one plane, one ruler; created by his own hands, his own blood, and a portion of his very essence.\n\nFrom his great keep, Malefacta, Lucifer waits for the day he can challenge for the Throne of Hell again.\" - translated from the ‘Infernal Grimoire: The Politics of Hell' Lilith begins combat by peppering her foes with her spell-like abilities.\n\nWhen combat begins, Lilith usually hits the closest opponents (she deems most susceptible) with her mass hold monster ability. Next she unleashes a fireball hoping to engulf as many opponents as possible. She then charges in with her longsword, peppering her foes with lightning bolts and fireballs. If she has time before battle begins, she uses her magic circle against good and her unholy aura on herself. Any foes slain in combat are subjected to her animate dead spell-like ability. Against powerful foes she summons other devils to fight with her.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"Amaheuris"},{"name":"Stone Treant","cr":16,"xp":76800,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","elemental","native"],"init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +15 natural, -2 size","hp":346,"hd":"21d10+210 (+21)","hdvalue":21,"fort":17,"ref":13,"will":17,"dr":"10/slashing and adamantine","immunities":["elemental traits"],"sr":31,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":5}],"melee":"6 slams +32 (3d8+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"acidic blood","details":"5d4 acid, DC 20 Reflex half"},{"type":"trample","details":"3d8+18, DC 32"}],"strength":35,"dexterity":8,"constitution":30,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":16,"charisma":12,"baseatk":21,"cmb":35,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush and sunder","cmd":44,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15,"special":"+21 in stony underground areas"}],"languages":["Sylvan","Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"radial symmetry"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","grove (2-16)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks much like an animated sculpture of a tree. It has a thick, corrugated hide of bark like stone, with many thick branches. It travels along on clusters of humping and twining stone roots. It possesses no discernible face.","group":"Treant","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acidic Blood","kind":"Ex","details":"Anyone striking the stone treant with a piercing or slashing attack and inflicting damage releases a gout of acidic blood, which causes 5d4 points of acid damage to the person who struck it. A DC 20 Reflex save reduces this damage by half. The blood becomes inert one round after leaving the elemental's body."},{"type":"Radial Symmetry","kind":"Ex","details":"Because of its shape, the stone treant can bring no more than four of its slam attacks to bear on any one target. However, it also perceives the area around it equally well, and thus it cannot be flanked."}],"description":"The stone treant is a variant of the treant native to the Plane of Earth. They are very rare even there, located in isolated pockets in the plane where they tend groves of crystals and natural gem outcroppings. Knowledge of their existence has been all but lost, as has the ritual of summoning and binding them into service.\n\nA stone treant stands 20-30 ft. tall, with a trunk about 4 ft. in diameter. It weighs close to 10,000 pounds.\n\nStone treants are intelligent, and speak Terran. They generally don't bother to communicate with non-earth elemental beings, however.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Wood Elemental","cr":16,"xp":76800,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","native"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +19 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"21d10+105","hdvalue":21,"fort":17,"ref":6,"will":15,"dr":"15/slashing","immunities":["elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +33 (3d6+13/19-20)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"flesh to wood","details":"touch +32, DC 21"},{"type":"forest mastery"}],"strength":37,"dexterity":8,"constitution":21,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":12,"charisma":12,"baseatk":21,"cmb":36,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. sunder","cmd":45,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. sunder","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (slam)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (slam)"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":24,"special":"+28 in forests"},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12,"special":"+28 in forests"},{"skill":"Survival","value":24}],"languages":["Sylvan"],"environments":["any forests","any jungles"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","stand (3-6)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Wood elementals appear as twiggy, wooden beings, with long, elf-like ears and curious features. They are quite strong, although slow moving and deliberate. Wood elementals encountered are always huge beings, and it isn't known if smaller versions exist.","group":"Elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Flesh to Wood","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds a wood elemental may attempt to turn flesh to wood with a successful touch attack. A DC 21 Fortitude save negates. The save is Constitution-based. This malady cannot be remedied short of a wish, miracle, or Dobrynya the druid's intervention."},{"type":"Forest Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"A wood elemental gains a +1 bonus to both attack and damage rolls if she and her opponent are both in a forested area. This ability has been added in to the above stat block."}],"description":"Wood elementals serve as protectors of the forest, and each forest usually has one, while great primeval forests may boast several. Wood elementals spend most of their time in a euphoric slumber, waking only when their forest is in danger. At these times the wood elemental moves forth to seek and destroy that which threatens the forest. At times they are known to ally with factions that work to protect and save the forest, especially elves. Wood elementals attack with a slam attack, as their limbs are strong and powerful, much like those of a treants.\n\nHuge wood elementals stand 16 to 24 ft. tall, with a 3 foot to 7 foot trunk, weighing 1,500 to 4,000 pounds. Wood elementals typically replicate the look of the native trees of their forest; some wood elementals appear as mighty oaks, some as maples, birch, pine or majestic cedar trees. More exotic species are certainly possible (tiger wood, ipe, etc.).","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Original author William Loran Christensen  Originally appearing in Fane of the Fallen (© Frog God Games/ William Loran Christensen, 2010)"},{"name":"Wyrm Gray Dragon","cr":16,"xp":76800,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (330 ft., DC 25)"],"ac":41,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":41,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +34 natural, -2 size","hp":310,"hd":"23d12+161","hdvalue":23,"fort":20,"ref":14,"will":20,"immunities":["paralysis","sleep"],"sr":27,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +33 (2d6+12), bite +34 (2d8+18/19-20), 2 wings +31 (1d8+6), tail slap +31 (2d6+18)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 22d6 fire; DC 28 Ref half"}],"spellsknown_caster_level":15,"spellsknown_concentration":22,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"power word blind"},{"spell":"waves of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"greater heroism"},{"spell":"move earth"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"cloudkill"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"transmute rock to mud"},{"spell":"wall of stone"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"scrying"},{"spell":"stoneskin"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"gaseous form"},{"spell":"protection from energy"},{"spell":"ray of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"eagle's splendor"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"protection from good"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"touch of fatigue"}]}],"strength":35,"dexterity":8,"constitution":25,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":21,"charisma":19,"baseatk":23,"cmb":37,"cmd":46,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":30},{"skill":"Fly","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":30},{"skill":"Perception","value":35},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":35},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":30},{"skill":"Stealth","value":17},{"skill":"Swim","value":46}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aquan","Common","Draconic","Giant Special Abilities"],"environments":["warm coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Steam emanates from the nostrils and mouth of this slate gray dragon.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A gray dragon's breath weapon is a superheated line of steam."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older gray dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Corrupt Water","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day an adult or older gray dragon can stagnate 10 cubic ft. of still water, making it foul and unable to support water-breathing life. The ability spoils liquids containing water. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC 19) or become ruined. This ability is the equivalent of a 1st-level spell. Its range is 180 ft."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A gray dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. • Young-fog cloud; • Juvenile-create water; • Old-control winds; • Ancient-control water;"},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A gray dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."}],"description":"Gray dragons are evil dragons that inhabit mountains and hills near coastlines. They have little regard for other races and often enslave others to do their bidding. Adult and older gray dragons are rarely found without a retinue of humanoid slaves. Gray dragons mate for life and a single mated pair often terrorizes nearby villages, laying waste to those that oppose the dragon's will.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Abyssal Harvester","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Gargantuan","type":"aberration","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":6,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+22 natural, -4 size","hp":283,"hd":"21d8+189","hdvalue":21,"fort":16,"ref":9,"will":15,"dr":"15/cold iron","immunities":["poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"6 tentacles +22 (4d6+15/19-20 plus grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"debilitating constrict"},{"type":"far reaching"},{"type":"harvest"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"plane shift","details":"Astral Plane, the Abyss, the Nine Hells, or the Material Plane only"}]}],"strength":41,"dexterity":10,"constitution":29,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":16,"charisma":13,"baseatk":15,"cmb":29,"cmb_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +6 vs. grapple","cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, grapple can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (tentacle)"},{"feat":"Improved Grapple"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (tentacle)"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tentacle)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":21},{"skill":"Perception","value":31},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":5},{"skill":"Survival","value":27}],"languages":["Abyssal"],"sq":[{"type":"tentacle regeneration"}],"environments":["any Abyss"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This gigantic beast stands at least 40 ft. tall. It is a squat, bloated mass of grayish, leathery flesh, somewhat oval in shape with six long, serpentine tentacles protruding from its form. A massive gaping maw dominates its top surface extending around its entire top half. Hundreds of smaller tentacles adorn the lower part of its body, apparently aiding in locomotion.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Debilitating Constriction","kind":"Su","details":": An abyssal harvester that has successfully grappled an opponent of its size or smaller deals tentacle damage plus 1d4 points of Constitution damage each round the hold is maintained. A creature reduced to Constitution 0 by an abyssal harvester dies. Note, that the abyssal harvester only deals Constitution damage when constricting a foe."},{"type":"Far Reaching","kind":"Su","details":": An abyssal harvester can remain on its abyssal plane and inject up to four of its tentacles across the dimensions and into the Ethereal Plane, Astral Plane, material planes, or Nine Hells. It can do this a total of twelve times per day (so it could inject one tentacle twelve times into any plane, or four tentacles up to three times each). All of its tentacles must be injected into the same plane, and all appear within the same 20-foot area. While using this abitliy, it uses sensory organs on its tentacles to see, hear, smell, and efel its surroundings. It can attack normally (at its full attack bonus) while using this ability but it cannot move from its current location. It can withdraw its tentacles as a move action and re-inject them into the same plane (or a different plane) on its next turn. A dismissal, dispel chaos, or dispel evil spell (using the second effect of either spell) causes an abyssal harvester to withdraw a single tentacle (whichever one was touched) if it fails its Wli lsave. It cannot re-inject that same tentacle into the same plane for one day. A banishment spell forces an abyssal harvester to withdraw all of its tentacles if it fails its Will save. It cannot re-inject any ten-tacles that were banished into the same plane for one day."},{"type":"Harvest","kind":"Su","details":": This ability can only be used when the abyssal harvester is on its abyssal plane and injects its tentacles into the Ethereal Plane, Astral Plane, a material plane, or the Nine Hells. A grappled foe with 20 or fewer hit points or 4 or fewer Constitution points must succeed on a DC 21 Will save or be drawn through an invisible planar gate (created around the abyssal harvester's tentacles) onto the same plane where the abyssal harvester currently resides. An opponent drawn into the same plane with the harvester is still grappled upon arrival. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Tentacle Regeneration","kind":"Ex","details":": An abyssal harvester regrows any lost tentacles in 1 week."}],"description":"Abyssal harvesters are horrid monsters found primarily on the Abyssal planes and rarely anywhere else (for an extended amount of time at least). They were created by foul and demonic magic to aid in harvesting bodies and living creatures from other planes for use by the various demon lords and princes (uses include slaves, food, concubines, and so on).\n\nAn abyssal harvester spends most of its time scouring the planes for potential prey. It does so by injecting a single tentacle into the plane and using it to survey its surroundings. If nothing of interest is located, the harvester withdraws its tentacle and moves on. Much of its time is spent scouring the planes as directed by a demon prince, lord, or other powerful demon (though abyssal harvesters loathe answering to non-princes and rarely do so unless said demon poses a direct threat to the harvester's existence). When not under the direct orders of a prince or demon, any creature a harvester harvests becomes a meal for itself.\n\nA typical abyssal harvester is 40 ft. tall, 20 ft. wide at its base, and weighs around 40 tons. Its flesh is gray and usually carries a stench of ozone.\n\nAbyssal harvesters are deadly opponents in battle and have no reservations about engaging an enemy in combat. The creature is smart enough to know when it is beaten however and will withdraw (using its plane shift ability) if combat is going against it.\n\nMost of the time however, an abyssal harvester simply injects its tentacles into a plane, grapples its foes, and when they are sufficiently weakened, draws them through a temporary gate onto its plane where it devours them.\n\nFoes can attack an abyssal harvester's tentacles. A tentacle has AC 21 (+11 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 21, and can withstand 30 points of damage. Damaging or severing a tentacle doesn't harm the abyssal harvester (damage dealt to a tentacle isn't subtracted from its hit points).\n\nAn abyssal harvester's natural weapons, as well as any weapons it wields, are treated as chaotic-aligned and evil-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Afanc","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"N","size":"Colossal","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"telepathy","modifier":"100 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +20 natural, -8 size","hp":333,"hd":"23d10+207","hdvalue":23,"fort":22,"ref":14,"will":11,"dr":"15/adamantine","immunities":["poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":28,"weaknesses":["water-dependant"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +32 (5d6+16), 2 claws +31 (2d8+16)","space":"100 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"sea swell"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"4d6+16 plus 8 points acid damage, AC 20, 33 hp"}],"strength":42,"dexterity":13,"constitution":28,"intelligence":3,"wisdom":15,"charisma":10,"baseatk":23,"cmb":47,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple, sunder","cmd":58,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Greater Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Swim","value":24}],"languages":["telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This massive creature appears to be a gray-skinned whale with a bulbous head similar to a catfish's. Its eyes are sullen and blue and its huge pectoral fins are serrated.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Sea Swell","kind":"Ex","details":": As a full-round action, an afanc can raise the front part of its body out of the water and bring it crashing back down against the surface. This generates massive waves up to 30 ft. tall that may capsize boats and ships within 100 ft. of the afanc. Boats and ships less than 20 ft. long automatically capsize. Boats over 20 ft. long may or may not capsize depending on the skill of the one piloting the vessel. A character steering or guiding a boat or ship over 20 ft. long that succeeds on a DC 37 Profession (sailor) check manages to keep the boat afloat; otherwise it capsizes, spilling its contents into the water. The check DC is Strength-based."}],"description":"Afancs are the sea monsters that sailors talk about when spinning tales of the sea. They are the creatures responsible for entire fleets and crews being lost or destroyed. They are thought by many to be the \"kings\" of the sea as most other water-dwellers pale in comparison both in strength and size to the mighty afanc.\n\nAfancs are omnivorous hunters of the deep sea, feeding on a mixed diet of kelp, coral, sea plants, sharks, whales, various other large fishes, and swimmers and sailors unfortunate enough to cross the path of an afanc.\n\nAfancs are sometimes worshipped as sea gods by small towns, villages, and seaside communities. Sacrifices to the \"Great Whale Gods\" include in various forms enormous amounts of cultivated sea plants, massive amounts of fish that have been netted, young girls or women, and occasionally an entire ship laden with criminals who are to be executed for their crimes.\n\nAn afanc is generally about 100 ft. long though specimens as large as 200 ft. long are thought to exist. Its whale-like body is colored gray or sometimes bluish-green and its eyes are always blue. Its tail is extremely long and ends in a truncated or flat, square edge. An afanc has a bulbous, somewhat flattened head, not unlike that of a great catfish.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ferrous Giant","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["info"],"ac":32,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":32,"ac_mods":"+6 armor, +18 natural, -2 size","hp":287,"hd":"25d8+175","hdvalue":25,"fort":21,"ref":8,"will":12,"dr":"15/cold iron","immunities":["fire","mind-affecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"greataxe +31 (4d6+22, 19-20/x3) or greatsword +31 (4d6+22, 17-20/x2); or 2 slams +31 (2d6+15 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"trample","details":"2d6+22; DC 37"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":22,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"heat metal"},{"spell":"levitate","details":"iron or steel objects or creatures only, including itself"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"wall of iron"}]}],"strength":40,"dexterity":11,"constitution":25,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":14,"baseatk":18,"cmb":35,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush, grapple, sunder","cmd":45,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. bull rush, sunder","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Greater Sunder"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (greatsword or greataxe)"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Craft [weaponsmithing])"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Craft (any one)","value":30},{"skill":"Craft (weaponsmithing)","value":36},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":27}],"languages":["Common","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"oversized weapon use"},{"type":"weapon and armor proficiency"}],"environments":["any mountains","temperate hills","warm hills"],"organizations":["solitary","family (2-4 plus 35% noncombatants plus 1 cleric or druid of 9th-12th level)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"A towering giant stands 20 ft. tall with dark, ruddy skin. His course brown hair and beard are long and wild, and he wears a thick breastplate and dozens of furs.","group":"Ferrous","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ferrous Mind","kind":"Ex","details":"Ferrous giants are immune to mindinfluencing effects (charms, compulsions, phantasms, patterns, and morale effects)."},{"type":"Pound","kind":"Ex","details":"A ferrous giant that successfully grabs a foe two or more sizes smaller than itself can smash the opponent into the ground, walls, nearby trees, or other solid objects as a standard action. This deals 2d6+22 points of bludgeoning damage to the victim. In addition, the opponent must make a successful DC 37 Fortitude save or be stunned for one round. A ferrous giant can perform this action once per round as long as it maintains the grapple. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Oversized Weapon Use","kind":"Ex","details":"A ferrous giant wields a Gargantuan greatsword or greataxe without penalty."},{"type":"Weapon and Armor Proficiency","kind":"Ex","details":"Ferrous giants are automatically proficient with simple weapons, martial weapons, light and medium armor, and shields."}],"description":"The great ferrous giant stands over 20 ft. tall and appears as a humanoid composed of flexible and bendable iron. Though it is often mistaken for a construct, it is in fact a very intelligent giant. A ferrous giant makes its home deep within a secluded mountain range. Its lair is often a deep cave or cavern or a gigantic castle constructed of iron and built into the face of a mountain. Ferrous giants are generally solitary creatures rarely interacting or dealing with other races, including other giants. Though not on bad terms with other giants, they simply have no interest in dealing with them. Ferrous giants spend most of their days hunting (deer, moose, boar, elk) and foraging or crafting exquisite weapons of iron. Some particularly sociable ferrous giants (a rare occurrence to be assured) set up a trading operation with a nearby town or city, exchanging weapons for whatever might interest the giant (food, iron, money, etc.). In melee, the ferrous giant uses its Huge iron battleaxe or longsword to bash or cleave its opponents. If disarmed, or if it is feeling particularly vile, a ferrous giant can pummel a foe with its massive fists. When fighting smaller foes, the ferrous giant often opens combat by trampling its foes or grabbing them and flinging them aside. Particularly noisome opponents are scooped up and pounded into the ground. The ferrous giant uses its heat metal ability in combat to heat the armor of its opponents and burn its foes.","as_character":[{"description":"Ferrous giants are extremely strong, have hardy constitutions and remain versatile all other facets. Ferrous giant shamans are usually adepts or druids. Clerics can choose two of the following domains: Earth, Fire, Knowledge, and Sun.","racial_traits":[{"type":"Ability Score Bonuses","value":"+30 Strength, +15 Constitution, +2 Intelligence, +2 Wisdom, +2 Charisma"},{"type":"Huge","value":"Ferrous giants are Huge and take a -2 penalty to AC, -2 penalty to attack rolls, +2 bonus to Combat Maneuver Bonus and Combat Maneuver Defense, and a -8 penalty to Stealth checks. A ferrous giant's lifting and carrying limits quadruple those of Medium characters. Space 15ft., Reach 15ft."},{"type":"Speed","value":"A ferrous giant's base speed is 50 ft."},{"type":"Low-light vision","value":"Ferrous giants can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light."},{"type":"Racial Hit Dice","value":"A ferrous giant starts with twenty-five levels of humanoid, which provide it with 25d8 HD, a base attack bonus of +18, and base save bonuses of Fort +14, Ref +8, Will +8."},{"type":"Racial Skills","value":"A ferrous giant's humanoid levels give it skill ranks equal to 25 x (2 + Int modifier). Its class skill are Craft (weapons), Intimidate, and Perception"},{"type":"Racial Feats","value":"A ferrous giant's giant levels give it 12 feats."},{"type":"AC","value":"+18 natural AC bonus."},{"type":"Natural Weapons","value":"Ferrous giants can fight with 2 unarmed strikes that deal lethal damage (2d6+15)."},{"type":"Special Attacks","value":"Grab, pound, spell-like abilities, trample."},{"type":"Special Qualities","value":"Damage reduction 15/cold iron, fire immunity, ferrous mind."},{"type":"Weapon and Armor Proficiency","value":"Ferrous giants are automatically proficient with simple weapons, martial weapons, light and medium armor, and shields."},{"type":"Languages","value":"Ferrous giants begin play speaking Giant and Common. Ferrous giants with high intelligence scores can choose from the following languages: Draconic, Elven, Goblin, and Orc."}]}],"ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"breastplate, Gargantuan greatsword or greataxe"},{"name":"Gelatinous Emperor","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"ooze","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":29,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"+21 natural, -2 size","hp":256,"hd":"19d8+171","hdvalue":19,"fort":17,"ref":8,"will":10,"dr":"10/magic and good","immunities":["acid","electricity","ooze traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":28,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"2 tentacles +23 (2d8+10 plus 2d8 acid)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"spew acid"},{"type":"trample","details":"2d8+15 plus 2d8 acid, DC 29"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 7, 1d4 black puddings 100%, 1d4 gelatinous cubes 100%, or 1d2 15 HD black puddings 50%"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":10,"constitution":28,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":15,"charisma":13,"baseatk":14,"cmb":26,"cmd":36,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tentacle)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":4},{"skill":"Stealth","value":1},{"skill":"Swim","value":19}],"languages":["Abyssal (cannot speak)"],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (1 emperor plus 2-5 advanced black puddings)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This large, reddish-brown amorphous blob moves slowly forward.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"A gelatinous emperor's acid doesn't harm metal or stone."},{"type":"Spew Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"A gelatinous emperor can, as a standard action, spew forth acid in a 30-foot line at a single target. A creature struck takes 12d6 points of acid damage. A DC 28 Reflex save reduces the damage by half. Once a gelatinous emperor has spewed acid, it cannot do so again for 1d4 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Gelatinous emperors are intelligent, foul oozes found in the court of Jubilex. What purpose and in what capacity they serve the Faceless Lord is anyone's guess. From his Abyssal plane they strike out, devouring anything and everything they run across. They are eternal hunters, always moving and always hungry. When a gelatinous emperor slips into the Material Plane it quickly ravages the area leaving it devoid of all life. Thankfully these creatures are not often found on the Material Plane.\n\nA gelatinous emperor is believed to be a foul mix of gelatinous cube, gray ooze, black pudding, and all other manner of puddings and oozes meshed together by Jubilex, either for some nefarious purpose or for nothing more than his sheer amusement. Sages believe the latter to be the truer of the two theories.\n\nA gelatinous emperor attacks by forming multiple pseudopods from its amorphous body and lashing out at its opponents. If the emperor can maneuver its opponents into a tight group it employs its trample attack, crushing as many of its foes in one move as possible.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Jack-in-irons Giant","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":28,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +19 natural, -2 size","hp":321,"hd":"26d8+204","hdvalue":26,"fort":23,"ref":11,"will":1,"defensive_abilities":["rock catching"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"spiked greatclub +31 (3d8+19 plus  daze) or great chain +31 (2d8+13 plus daze) or  2 slams +30 (2d6+13 plus daze)","ranged":"rock +19 (2d6+19)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"daze"},{"type":"pound"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"140 ft."},{"type":"shake the earth"},{"type":"trample","details":"2d6+19, DC 36"}],"strength":36,"dexterity":12,"constitution":26,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":14,"charisma":11,"baseatk":19,"cmb":0,"cmd":12,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Sunder"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Martial Weapon Proficiency (great chain)"},{"feat":"Martial Weapon Proficiency (greatclub)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (greatclub)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (chain)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":25},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Survival","value":11}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["temperate forests","temperate plains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"Brutish, warty, hairy, and stinking of oil and iron, this creature has a jutting lower jaws and tusk like teeth, not unlike an orc or hobgoblin of huge size wrapped in chains of iron. It wears belts of skulls and rotting heads about its throat and waist.","group":"Giant","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Daze","kind":"Ex","details":"Any creature hit by a jack-in-iron's melee attack must succeed on a DC 36 Fortitude save or be dazed 1d2 rounds. The save DC is Strength-based and is a function of the jack-in-irons not its weapon(s)."},{"type":"Pound","kind":"Ex","details":"A jack-in-irons that makes a successful grapple check against a foe two or more sizes smaller than itself can smash the opponent into the ground, walls, nearby trees, or other solid objects as a standard action. This deals 2d6+19 points of bludgeoning damage to the victim. In addition, the opponent must succeed on a DC 36 Fortitude save or be stunned for one round. A jack-in-irons can perform this action once per round as long as it maintains the grapple. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Shake the Earth","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a jack-in-irons can stomp its foot on the ground causing powerful vibrations to radiate out around the giant. Any creature within 5 ft. of the jack-in-irons must succeed on a DC 36 Reflex save or fall prone. The save DC is Strength-based."}],"description":"The jacks-in irons enjoy fastening gate chains and portcullis chains around their wrists, fore-arms and shins and tie chains about their throats, shoulders and waists which hang with the heads of their many victims.\n\nJacks-in-irons frequently operate as highwaymen, making their dwellings in ruined towers along abandoned roads. From this base they roam out along old country trails ambushing unwary travelers, trade caravans and the knights assigned to protect them. They are known to take prisoners and hold them for high ransom.\n\nOrcs and goblins often follow a jack-in-irons as their king or leader due to its massive size, brute strength, and penchant for wickedness-all of which are things that such evil creatures admire.\n\nA jack-in-irons stands 20 to 25 ft. tall and weighs 13,000 to 15,000 pounds. It prefers to dress in dark colors such as black or brown and always wears a multitude of chains about its body (as bracelets, necklaces, or slung about its shoulders). Its hair is dark and matted and many male jack-in-irons sport thick, bushy beards. Its eyes are purplish-black with light green irises.\n\nJack-in-irons speak Giant.\n\nBull rush, Awesome blow, bash, bash, bash, cleave, rinse and repeat if necessary until they are out of attacks or out of enemies. Jacks-in-irons think of themselves as invincible and fight to the death.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"spiked greatclub, great chain"},{"name":"Royal Time Elemental","cr":17,"xp":102400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","time"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":21,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 insight, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":228,"hd":"24d10+96","hdvalue":24,"fort":14,"ref":21,"will":22,"defensive_abilities":["foresight"],"dr":"15/-","immunities":["elemental traits","temporal magic"],"sr":28,"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":20,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +28 (2d6+4 plus cell death)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"alter age","details":"2/day, Fort DC 26"},{"type":"multi-manifestation"},{"type":"temporal displacement","details":"3/day, 24 minutes, Fort DC 26"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":24,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":28,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon time elementals","details":"9th level, 1d4 common time elementals, 70%, or 1-2 noble time elementals 30%"},{"spell":"time stop"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":20,"constitution":18,"intelligence":22,"wisdom":22,"charisma":20,"baseatk":24,"cmb":29,"cmd":51,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Natural Attack (slam)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":29},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":38},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":39},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":28},{"skill":"Survival","value":33}],"languages":["telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"time jaunt","details":"DC 26"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Time)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (noble plus 1-2 common time elementals)","court (royal plus 1-2 nobles and 1-4 common time elementals)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a formless cloud of yellowish-red vapor or dust about 5 ft. in diameter.","group":"Elemental","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alter Age","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day, a noble time elemental can age a creature simply by touching it (this requires a melee touch attack). If successful, the target must succeed on a Fortitude save or advance forward one aging step (from adulthood to middle age, from middle age to old, from old to venerable, and so on). If a character ages, he takes all the effects to his physical ability scores, but doesn't gain any of the bonuses to his mental ability scores. A venerable creature affected by this ability dies (from massive cell death) and cannot be restored to life by mortal magic. The save DC is Constitution-based. Alternately, a time elemental can use its alter age ability to reduce a character's age. If the target is unwilling, the time elemental must succeed on a melee touch attack. An unwilling target can make a Fortitude save to avoid the effects. If the save fails, the target ages one age step backwards (from middle age to adulthood for example) and gains all bonuses to physical ability scores from his new age (simply flip the penalties listed on the aging table into an equal numbered bonus). A character that regresses in age doesn't reduce its mental ability scores. This ability doesn't affect a character that has died from old age. A time elemental can also use this ability to age vegetable matter 10-200 years (older or younger) or mineral matter 100-2,000 years (older or younger). Royal time elementals can use this ability twice per day."},{"type":"Cell Death","kind":"Ex","details":"Damage dealt by a time elemental's slam attack doesn't heal naturally (but it can still be healed magically). Additionally, a creature slain by a time elemental can only be raised through the successful casting of a miracle, true resurrection, or wish spell."},{"type":"Foresight","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental can see a few seconds into the future. This ability prevents it from being surprised, caught flat-footed, or flanked. It also grants the time elemental an insight bonus to AC equal to its Wisdom bonus. This ability can be negated, but the time elemental can restart it as a free action on its next turn."},{"type":"Immunity to Temporal Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"Time elementals are immune to all time-related spells and effects (including time stop, temporal stasis, and the like). Note, the time stop ability of the noble and royal time elementals can affect those time elementals of lesser power (i.e., a noble can affect a common and a royal can affect a noble or common)."},{"type":"Multi-Manifestation","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental exists in several other dimensions at any given time. As a standard action, it can bring forth 1d4 of these manifestations to its current locale in order to gain multiple attacks that round. Treat each manifestation as a separate time elemental with hit points equal to the time elemental's current hit points. A manifestation cannot use any of the supernatural or spell-like abilities of the time elemental (a manifestation does however gain the time elemental's foresight ability). A time elemental cannot have more than four manifestations present at one time. Because each manifestation is a part of the time elemental that called them, a successful attack on the time elemental or any of its manifestations deals an equal amount of damage to them all."},{"type":"Summon Time Elementals","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day, a royal time elemental can attempt to summon 1d4 common time elementals with a 70% chance of success or 1-2 noble time elementals with a 30% chance of success. This ability is the equivalent of a 9th-level spell."},{"type":"Temporal Displacement","kind":"Su","details":"By making a melee touch attack against a foe, a noble or royal time elemental can remove that creature from the current time stream if it fails a Fortitude save. The save is Constitution-based. On a failed save, the creature disappears in a flash of white energy. For a number of minutes equal to the time elemental's Hit Dice, the displaced creature is effectively nonexistent. No form of magic, effect, or force can detect or aid such a creature. A displaced creature can attempt a Wisdom check (DC equal to the initial Fort DC) on its turn to break the effects and end the displacement. The save is Constitution-based. When the effect ends, the creature reappears in the same space it was in before being displaced. If the space is occupied when the creature returns, it is shunted aside to the first open space and takes no damage. A noble or royal time elemental can use this ability three times per day."},{"type":"Time Jaunt","kind":"Su","details":"A time elemental can slip through the time stream and appear anywhere on the same plane of existence as if by greater teleport. This ability transports the time elemental and up to four other creatures within a 30-foot radius. Unwilling creatures can attempt a Will save to avoid being carried away. This ability is otherwise similar to the spell of the same name (caster level equal to the elemental's HD). The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Time Stop","kind":"Sp","details":"Noble and royal time elementals can create an effect identical to a time stop spell once per day (caster level equals the time elemental's HD)."}],"description":"Time elementals are creatures from a plane most sages are unaware even exists. A time elemental is a powerful creature formed of pure time and matter such as is unknown to even the most learned of sages. It is unknown how or why time elementals enter the Material Plane, as they cannot be summoned using the standard summoning spells. Time elementals attack by forming misty or smoky arms from their forms and lashing at opponents or by spraying a fine mist onto their opponents so as to induce aging. Against particularly powerful opponents, a time elemental uses its alter age ability or (if of the royal sort) summons additional time elementals to its aid.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Time Elemental originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Choronzon Demon","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["confusion (10 ft., DC 24)"],"ac":32,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +22 natural, -2 size","hp":290,"hd":"20d10+180","hdvalue":20,"fort":23,"ref":14,"will":10,"dr":"10/cold iron and good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":29,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +30 (2d8+11/19-20), 2 claws +29 (1d8+11 plus daze)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 10d6 damage, Fort DC 29 half, usable every 1d4 rounds"},{"type":"daze","details":"claw attack, Fort DC 31 negates, dazed 1d3 rounds"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":29,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 5, 1d4 hezrous, 1d4 nalfeshnees, or 2d4 vrocks 35%"},{"spell":"word of chaos"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"chaos hammer"},{"spell":"unholy aura"},{"spell":"unholy blight"}]}],"strength":33,"dexterity":15,"constitution":29,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":18,"baseatk":20,"cmb":33,"cmd":45,"feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":27},{"skill":"Climb","value":34},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":25},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":39},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":25},{"skill":"Survival","value":22}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","band (choronzon plus 6-11 vrocks)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature stands at least 20 ft. tall with a huge, muscular body. Its massive arms and legs end in wicked claws. Its rounded, squat head, sits atop an extremely thick, almost nonexistent neck. The creature's gaping maw is filled with sharp fangs. Two large swept back horns jut from its head just above its rounded eyes.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Aura of Confusion","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by that choronzon's aura of confusion for one day. Other demons are immune to the choronzon's aura of confusion. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a choronzon can breathe forth a cone of bluish gas in a 40-foot cone. The gas lingers in the area for 1d2 rounds before dispersing. A creature killed by a choronzon's breath weapon has its body break apart into its individual protons, neutrons, and electrons. Creatures killed in this manner can only be restored to life by a miracle, wish, or true resurrection spell. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Choronzons are the demons of confusion, dispersion, and ultimate chaos. They are huge behemoths seemingly bred for war and battle, though most rarely take part in the Abyssal wars that rage between the planes. Choronzons prefer to use their talents on weak-minded creatures such as those that inhabit the Material planes, and as such, they are usually encountered there. These demons derive great pleasure in laying waste to villages and towns and even small kingdoms (if the mood strikes them).\n\nAmongst demonkind, choronzons are both feared and hated. A great enmity exists between balors and choronzons that scholars and lorekeepers can document, but cannot determine the source of the hatred between these two demonic races.\n\nA choronzon stands about 20 ft. tall and weighs about 9,000 pounds.\n\nIts scaly flesh is bluish-black and its eyes are crimson. Its horns are darker than the rest of its body and the creature's claws are pitch black. Its teeth are dull ivory in color.\n\nA choronzon begins combat by surrounding itself with its aura of confusion and then unleashing its breath weapon at its foes. Creatures surviving either attack are subjected to its word of chaos. Opponents that continue to press the battle are met with a mix of physical attacks and spell-like abilities. When it uses its Power Attack feat, a choronzon usually takes a -8 penalty on its attack rolls in order to gain a +8 bonus on its damage rolls.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Elemental Air Dragon","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","elemental","extraplanar"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":32,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"24d10+120","hdvalue":24,"fort":13,"ref":22,"will":16,"defensive_abilities":["air mastery"],"dr":"15/magic and silver","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":120,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +31 (2d8+12), 2 claws +31 (2d6+8), 2 wings +28 (1d8+8), tail slap +28 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 29, 10d8 fire"},{"type":"cyclone","details":"30 ft. radius, DC 27, 3d6 bludgeoning"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"control winds"}]}],"strength":26,"dexterity":27,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":24,"cmb":34,"cmd":52,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (breath weapon)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":29},{"skill":"Survival","value":29}],"languages":["Auran","Common"],"environments":["any (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This massive creature resembles a huge dragon composed of air and vapor. Its great wings are translucent and look like wisps of smoke. Its eyes are hollow sockets of mist though a glint of bright sunlight can occasionally be seen dancing across the surface. Its great tail appears as wisps of smoke or vapor and seems to trail off into nothingness.","group":"Elemental Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against an elemental air dragon."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"An elemental air dragon's breath weapon is a 50 ft. cone of superheated air."},{"type":"Cyclone","kind":"Ex","details":"By beating its wings rapidly back and forth, a hovering elemental air dragon can create a cyclone-like force of wind in a 30-foot radius around its body. This cyclone has the following effects: movement through the cyclone is one-quarter normal, ranged attacks suffer a -8 circumstance penalty in the area, and all nonmagical unprotected flames are automatically extinguished. Large or smaller creatures in the area must succeed on a DC 27 Reflex save or take 3d6 points of bludgeoning damage each round they remain in the area. Medium or smaller creatures in the area must succeed on a second Reflex save (same DC) or be knocked prone and back 1d4 x 10 ft., taking 1d6 points of nonlethal damage per 10 ft. Flying creatures are automatically grounded in this area. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"The Plane of Air is home to many creatures. Yet none are as feared as the elemental air dragons. Their great form and majestic aura strike fear into the bravest of souls. Elemental air dragons are as evil as their brethren (the other elemental dragons) and take joy and pride in swooping over a settlement or village and destroying it with their great wing buffet. Watching the frightened creatures flee in terror provokes some sort of perverse excitement in these dragons. Luckily, elemental air dragons rarely enter the Material Plane. Elemental air dragons dislike cloud dragons and mist dragons and seek to slay them whenever they are encountered. The average air elemental dragon is 30 ft. long. Elemental air dragons attack by swooping on their prey, unleashing a blast of superheated air, and then flying away. An elemental air dragon rarely, if ever, touches the ground. It often employs its cyclone buffet to knock more powerful creatures prone, then swoops in to blast them with its breath weapon or rend them with its claws and bite.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Elemental Water Dragon","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"outsider","subtypes":["elemental","extraplanar","water"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +16 natural, -2 size","hp":252,"hd":"24d10+120","hdvalue":24,"fort":13,"ref":17,"will":15,"defensive_abilities":["water mastery"],"dr":"10/magic and silver","immunities":["elemental traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":90}],"melee":"bite +32 (2d8+13), 2 claws +32 (2d6+9), 2 wings +29 (1d8+9), tail slap +29 (2d6+13)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50 ft. cone, DC 29, 14d8 fire"},{"type":"capsize"},{"type":"drench"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"control water"}]}],"strength":29,"dexterity":16,"constitution":20,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":24,"cmb":35,"cmd":51,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (breath weapon)"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Snatch"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":27},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":27},{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Survival","value":28},{"skill":"Swim","value":21}],"languages":["Aquan","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"transparency"}],"environments":["any (Plane of Water)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a massive dragon composed entirely of water. Its wings slosh and drip water as it moves them. Its great mouth opens into a maw of inky darkness. Water drips from its fangs.","group":"Elemental Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"The breath weapon of an elemental water dragon is a 50 ft. cone of superheated steam. This breath weapon is effective both on the surface and underwater."},{"type":"Capsize","kind":"Ex","details":"An elemental water dragon can attempt to capsize a boat or ship by ramming it as a charge attack and making a CMB check. The DC of this check is 25, or the result of the boat captain's Profession (sailor) check, whichever is higher. For each size category larger than the elemental water dragon's size, it takes a cumulative -10 penalty on this CMB check."},{"type":"Drench","kind":"Ex","details":"The elemental water dragon's touch puts out torches, campfires, exposed lanterns, and other open flames of nonmagical origin if these are of Large size or smaller. The creature can dispel magical fire it touches as dispel magic (caster level equals elemental's HD)."},{"type":"Water Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"An elemental water dragon gains a +1 bonus on attack and damage rolls if both it and its foes are touching water. If the opponent or elemental water dragon is touching the ground, the elemental water dragon takes a -4 penalty on attack and damage rolls. (These modifiers are not included in the statistics block.)"},{"type":"Transparency","kind":"Ex","details":"When submerged, an elemental water dragon is effectively invisible (DC 35 Perception check when near the surface only) until it attacks."}],"description":"From the Plane of Water comes the elemental water dragon (also called water wyrm by some sages). They make their homes in the deep oceans of the Material Plane and are rarely found far away from large expanses of water. An elemental water dragon is composed entirely of water and commands respect from the more intelligent sea creatures as well as those humanoids that ply their trade upon the waters. Elemental water dragons are evil and take great pleasure in demanding sacrifice from those that dare enter their realm. If the sacrifice placates the dragon, it lets the creature pass unabated; otherwise, it attacks with all of its might and most often destroys those that offend it or fail to appease its desires. Water dragons take great pleasure in capsizing and sinking ships. Particularly evil water dragons may accept a sacrifice and then sink the ship of those that crossed its path anyway. On occasion, a group of skum or other evil aquatic creatures can be found allied with an elemental water dragon, but this alliance is usually short-lived and often shaky. It generally ends with the elemental water dragon feeding on its former allies. Elemental water dragons prefer to fight in or near water where they can use their transparency and water mastery abilities to full advantage. They prefer to attack from ambush, often lying in wait for their opponents and then springing from the waves to assault their foes.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Ghaggurath","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"aberration","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":31,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +18 natural, -2 size","hp":304,"hd":"21d8+210","hdvalue":21,"fort":19,"ref":12,"will":20,"defensive_abilities":["resistant to poison"],"dr":"15/-","immunities":["charm","fear","paralysis","sleep"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":20},{"type":"cold","value":20},{"type":"fire","value":20},{"type":"sonic","value":20}],"sr":29,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"8 bites +27 (2d6+13/19-20 plus grab)","ranged":"4 thrall worms +18 (1d8 plus poison)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft. (30 ft. with tentacle)","special_attacks":[{"type":"thrall"}],"strength":37,"dexterity":21,"constitution":30,"intelligence":24,"wisdom":22,"charisma":21,"baseatk":15,"cmb":30,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":45,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Bleeding Critical"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":26},{"skill":"Climb","value":45},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":29},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (any)","value":31},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":28},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":28},{"skill":"Perception","value":36},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":21},{"skill":"Survival","value":30},{"skill":"Swim","value":22}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","Giant","Goblin","Infernal","Terran","Undercommon","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This massive creature appears to be a pile of brownish-gray flesh covered in large eyes. Eight long tentacles sprout from its body, each ending in a mouth lined with sharpened fangs. Its large central mass is amoeba-like and oozes a foul-smelling liquid.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Thrall worm-injury; save DC 30 Fort; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d6 Wisdom damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Resistance to Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"A ghaggurath is highly resistant to poison. Whenever it makes a saving throw against poison, it can roll its save twice, keeping the better result."},{"type":"Spittle","kind":"Ex","details":"In lieu of biting, a tentacle mouth can eject a fleshy worm, called a thrall worm, at a single target to a range of 50 ft. A target that is hit is automatically bitten by the worm and subjected to the ghaggurath's poison. Regardless of which head fires the worm, a ghaggurath can launch only 24 such worms in any 24-hour period. When a thrall worm strikes its target, it quickly burrows into the target's body. This worm can be safely removed with a successful DC 30 Heal check or by the application of a cure spell; otherwise removing the worm deals an extra 1d6 points of damage to the target. After 1d4 rounds, the worm works its way so deep into the target's body that it can only be removed by cutting open the area (dealing 1d8 points of damage to the victim) before attempting a Heal check or casting a cure spell. A remove disease spell destroys the worm if the caster succeeds on a caster level check against DC 30. As long as a thrall worm remains inside a target, the target cannot heal the Wisdom damage dealt by the ghaggurath's poison. A creature can only ever have one thrall worm inside it at one time; it can however be attacked by and bitten by multiple thrall worms. The check DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Thrall","kind":"Su","details":"A victim whose Wisdom score drops to 0 from the ghaggurath's poison is automatically dominated (as by a dominate monster spell, CL 20th). This effect lasts until the thrall worm is removed and at least 1 point of Wisdom is restored. The ghaggurath doesn't have to concentrate each day to maintain this effect, and a dominated creature doesn't receive a save to break the effects. If the ghaggurath is slain, any thrall under its command fall unconscious and remain so until the thrall worm is removed and at least 1 point of Wisdom is restored."}],"description":"The ghaggurath is a massive subterranean creature feared for its ability to enslave others to its will, and feared for its ability to devour just about anything it desires. Though the ghaggurath has a seemingly endless hunger, it can in fact go up to 6 months without a meal; its body enters a sort of hibernation to sustain the creature. During this time, many creatures assume the ghaggurath is vulnerable; it isn't. Though the creature appears to be hibernating, it is completely aware of its surroundings. Many would-be predators and foolish adventurers have stumbled upon a hibernating ghaggurath assuming it unaware, only to become the creature's next meal.\n\nResourceful adventurers who have braved the subterranean worlds tell of huge cities governed by ghagguraths and whose entire populations are enslaved and under command of these creatures. Other tales speak of an underground race of humans that worship the ghaggurath as deities. Most subterranean races fear these creatures and avoid them at all costs.\n\nIn combat, a ghaggurath lashes out with its tentacles, the mouths biting and gnashing its opponents. A grabbed foe is held and subjected to multiple bites. Stronger opponents, particularly spellcasters, are of great interest to a ghaggurath, and it usually subjects such opponents to its thrall worms, attempting to bring them under its control. Controlled spellcasters are forced to do the ghaggurath's bidding or carried back to their great underground cities, enslaved, and experimented upon. Eventually, when a ghaggurath grows weary of the creature, it devours it.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Great Wyrm Gray Dragon","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Gargantuan","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (360 ft., DC 27)"],"ac":42,"ac_touch":5,"ac_flat_footed":42,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +37 natural, -4 size","hp":362,"hd":"25d12+200","hdvalue":25,"fort":22,"ref":15,"will":22,"immunities":["paralysis","sleep"],"sr":29,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":250,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +34 (2d6+13), bite +35 (2d8+19/19-20), 2 wings +32 (2d6+6), tail slap +32 (2d8+19)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft. (20 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"120-ft. line, 24d6 fire; DC 30 Ref half"}],"spellsknown_caster_level":17,"spellsknown_concentration":25,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":8,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"horrid wilting"},{"spell":"moment of prescience"}]},{"spell_level":7,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"limited wish"},{"spell":"power word blind"},{"spell":"waves of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":6,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"flesh to stone"},{"spell":"greater heroism"},{"spell":"move earth"}]},{"spell_level":5,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"cloudkill"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"transmute rock to mud"},{"spell":"wall of stone"}]},{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dimension door"},{"spell":"greater invisibility"},{"spell":"scrying"},{"spell":"stoneskin"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"gaseous form"},{"spell":"protection from energy"},{"spell":"ray of exhaustion"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"eagle's splendor"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"locate object"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"burning hands"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"protection from good"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"touch of fatigue"}]}],"strength":37,"dexterity":8,"constitution":27,"intelligence":21,"wisdom":23,"charisma":21,"baseatk":25,"cmb":42,"cmd":51,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":33},{"skill":"Fly","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":33},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":33},{"skill":"Perception","value":38},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":38},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Swim","value":49},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":33}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aquan","Common","Draconic","Giant","Infernal Special Abilities"],"environments":["warm coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Steam emanates from the nostrils and mouth of this slate gray dragon.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A gray dragon's breath weapon is a superheated line of steam."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older gray dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Corrupt Water","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day an adult or older gray dragon can stagnate 10 cubic ft. of still water, making it foul and unable to support water-breathing life. The ability spoils liquids containing water. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC 19) or become ruined. This ability is the equivalent of a 1st-level spell. Its range is 180 ft."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A gray dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. • Young-fog cloud; • Juvenile-create water; • Old-control winds; • Ancient-control water;"},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A gray dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."}],"description":"Gray dragons are evil dragons that inhabit mountains and hills near coastlines. They have little regard for other races and often enslave others to do their bidding. Adult and older gray dragons are rarely found without a retinue of humanoid slaves. Gray dragons mate for life and a single mated pair often terrorizes nearby villages, laying waste to those that oppose the dragon's will.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Requiem Beetle","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"vermin","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"100 ft."}],"ac":31,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +24 natural, -4 size","hp":345,"hd":"30d8+210","hdvalue":30,"fort":24,"ref":11,"will":10,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["acid","mind-affecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"2 claws +29 (2d8+11 plus grab), bite +29 (2d10+11)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"4d6+11"},{"type":"earth-shaking"},{"type":"trample","details":"2d8+16, DC 36"}],"strength":33,"dexterity":12,"constitution":24,"wisdom":11,"charisma":2,"baseatk":22,"cmb":37,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":48,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Power Attack","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":1,"special":"(+9 jump) Perception +8"}],"environments":["any underground","warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This massive beetle has a dark red carapace, blackish-red wing covers, and black legs. Two large claw-like pincers protrude from its front slashing and ripping the very air around the creature. Its oversized mandibles are dark reddish-black.","group":"Beetle","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Earth-Shaking","kind":"Ex","details":": Whenever a requiem beetle moves more than 10 ft. in a round, all creatures within 10 ft. of the requiem beetle must succeed on a DC 34 Reflex save or fall prone. The save DC is Strength-based."}],"description":"Requiem beetles are beetles of enormous size reaching lengths of 100 ft. or more. They make their lairs in remote mountainous regions or deep underground in massive caverns. A typical lair contains a solitary creature (no two have ever been encountered together). Mating and reproduction rituals and methods among requiem beetles are unknown to sages, though it is generally accepted that requiem beetles follow other similar beetle and vermin mating patterns.\n\nThese monsters sustain themselves on a diet of mosses, funguses, lichens, molds, and oozes. Their natural immunity to acid allows them to kill and digest most oozes without bother. Requiem beetles are mindless hunters, like other vermin, and simply kill and eat whatever they come across. When they deplete an area of its food source they simply move to another location.\n\nRequiem beetles measure about 40 ft. long and weigh about 18 tons.\n\nA requiem beetle charges into combat attempting to trample as many of its opponents as it can. It uses its massive pincers in battle to cut and tear its opponents or grab and squeeze them. Once a requiem beetle grabs a foe it rarely lets go until either it or the opponent is dead. If forced to flee, a requiem beetle doesn't release its prey, but instead, carries it off with it.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Slorath","cr":18,"xp":153600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Gargantuan","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["cold"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +16 natural, -4 size","hp":250,"hd":"20d10+140","hdvalue":20,"fort":19,"ref":17,"will":10,"immunities":["cold"],"sr":32,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +26 (2d8+15)","ranged":"paralysis ray +20 (paralysis)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"paralyzing gaze"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"glacial storm","details":"as meteor storm, but deals cold damage; half"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"cone of cold"},{"spell":"freezing sphere","details":"half"},{"spell":"ice storm"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":17,"constitution":24,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":20,"cmb":34,"cmd":47,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Gaze to Ray"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Bullrush"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (ray)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":14},{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":26},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14,"special":"+24 in arctic environments"},{"skill":"Swim","value":20}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Giant"],"environments":["cold hills","cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"Slithering from the snow emerges a 40-foot long serpent with glossy-white scales and a bluish-white underbelly, its long, slender, icy-blue tongue flickering. Its vertical-slit pupils glow an otherworldly greenish-blue and rows of sharpened teeth line tremendous mouth.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Paralyzing Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Paralysis 1d6 +4 rounds, 30 ft., Fortitude DC 22 negates. The save is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Paralysis","kind":"Su","details":"Alternately, a slorath can use its Gaze to Ray feat to release a ray of paralysis (range of 30 ft.) as a ranged touch attack. After using its gaze attack in this manner, the slorath cannot use its paralyzing gaze for 1d4 rounds and it is disoriented during this time (-2 penalty on attack rolls, saves, skill checks, and ability checks). The save is Charisma-based."}],"description":"The great sloraths are found only in the coldest and most desolate regions, though close enough to civilization to hunt and stage raids against humanoid settlements when the slorath goes hunting. Highly intelligent and aware, the slorath is a fierce predator that defends its hunting ground with precision tactics and power. Small villages within a slorath's territory sometimes strike deals with these creatures; offering sacrifices in return for the protection the slorath can offer.\n\nSlorath are generally nocturnal carnivores. They exist on a diet of white dragons, polar bears, frost men (see entry in this book), and barbegazi (see entry in this book). They are particularly fond of white dragon meat and often go out of their way to hunt for such creatures. Frost giants often strike deals with frost giants so it isn't uncommon for the two to be encountered together working toward a common goal.\n\nSlorath lairs are either enormous tunnels deep under the ice and snow or abandoned white dragon lairs. Encounters are almost always with a solitary creature. In rare instances young sloraths or eggs might be found in a lair. Young slorath resemble their parent in all respects. Slorath eggs are stark white in color.\n\nA slorath usually begins an encounter by hiding under the snow waiting for prey to wander by, or by lying unmoving on the snow itself where its coloration offers it camouflage against the white background. When prey comes within range, the slorath assaults it with its paralyzing gaze.\n\nHelpless creatures are then attacked with its powerful bite. Those that attempt to avoid its gaze witness the slorath project its gaze as a ray of blue energy (using the Gaze to Ray feat).\n\nContinued aggression against a slorath results in it unleashing a cone of cold or ice storm on its foes. If faced with particularly powerful foes, it uses its ice storm and glacial storm special abilities. A slorath doesn't fight to the death and flees if combat goes against it. Note however, if young slorath are present and they are threatened, a slorath fights to the death.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Demoriel","cr":19,"xp":204800,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect good"},{"type":"detect magic"},{"type":"see invisibility"}],"ac":40,"ac_touch":25,"ac_flat_footed":35,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +15 natural, +10 profane","hp":210,"hd":"20d10+100","hdvalue":20,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (good, silver)"],"fort":11,"ref":17,"will":6,"save_mods":"+2 on all saves from spells and effects from good-aligned creatures","defensive_abilities":["resistant to good magic"],"dr":"15/good and silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":30,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"+3 unholy short sword +30 (1d6+9/19- 20) or 2 claws +26 (1d6+6)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"enrapture"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":25,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blasphemy"},{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fireball"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"magic circle against good"},{"spell":"major image"},{"spell":"polymorph","details":"self only"},{"spell":"suggestion"},{"spell":"unholy aura"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"meteor swarm"},{"spell":"power word stun"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 9, 1d6 erinyes or 1d2 barbed devils 100% or 1 horned devil 60%"},{"spell":"wall of fire"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":21,"constitution":20,"intelligence":23,"wisdom":23,"charisma":31,"baseatk":20,"cmb":12,"cmd":27,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (fireball)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (short sword)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":45},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":45},{"skill":"Disguise","value":37},{"skill":"Fly","value":28},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":37},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":29},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":26},{"skill":"Perception","value":33},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":33},{"skill":"Stealth","value":28},{"skill":"Survival","value":26}],"languages":["Abyssal","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Giant","Ignan","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Infernus)"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (Demoriel plus 1-4 horned devils)"],"treasure":"double standard","description_visual":"This creature is a very attractive female with raven black hair, coal black eyes, amber skin, and a shapely form. Small bat wings protrude from her shoulders, and tiny horns jut from her forehead, just above her eyes.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Enrapture","kind":"Su","details":"Those viewing Demoriel must succeed on a DC 30 Will save or stand enthralled for 1 minute. This functions as a hold person spell (caster level 20th). An affected creature can attempt a new Will save each round to break the effects. The save DC is Charisma-based. A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected by Demoriel's enrapture for one day. Reaver: Reaver is Demoriel's finely crafted +3 unholy short sword."}],"description":"Demoriel was once a powerful angel that made her home in the heavens among the other angels. In the Celestial Hierarchy she was a member of the Cherubim and served alongside Gabriel, Raphael, and Ophaniel. During the Unholy Schism, she sided with Lucifer and aided him by seducing another Cherub wherein Lucifer caught the angel unaware and murdered him on the spot. When Lucifer was thrown down from the good-aligned planes, Demoriel was beside him; cast out for the sin of slaying another angel and spilling the blood of an angel in the outer planes. When Lucifer envisioned Hell, Demoriel envisioned herself on the throne next to him, serving as Hell's Queen. Unfortunately for her, she became one of his many concubines but never his bride, for the Great Uprising occurred in Hell and the other arch-devils moved to destroy Lucifer and his court. When Lucifer was removed from Hell's Throne and took up residence in a pocket plane called Infernus, Demoriel followed. Once again, she was denied her place on the throne next to Lucifer as he took a devil named Shabiri as his consort. Though Demoriel remains ever loyal to Lucifer, she doesn't trust nor like Shabiri. For now she waits until her time comes when she can discredit or destroy Shabiri and replace her as Lucifer's consort. Though Lucifer no longer rules Hell, Demoriel still serves him unswervingly. She follows no other, though she is more than willing to lead other creatures to their demise by feigning loyalty to them. She has a particularly vile hatred for celestials (more than other devils do it seems) and enjoys corrupting and destroying them. Demoriel attacks with her spell-like abilities, attempting to charm the strongest opponents she faces. If forced into melee, she attacks with her spell-like abilities and short sword or summons other devils to fight for her while she maintains a position away from the immediate fight.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"Reaver"},{"name":"Leviathan","cr":19,"xp":204800,"alignment":"N","size":"Colossal","type":"magical beast","init":-2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":0,"ac_flat_footed":30,"ac_mods":"-2 Dex, +30 natural, -8 size","hp":310,"hd":"20d10+200","hdvalue":20,"fort":24,"ref":10,"will":12,"dr":"20/magic","immunities":["cold","electricity"],"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":20},{"type":"sonic","value":20}],"sr":30,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +34 (6d6+22/19-20), tail slap +29 (4d6+11)","space":"30 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"capsize"},{"type":"smashing breach"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"6d8+22 acid damage, AC 25, 31 hp"},{"type":"tail storm"},{"type":"whale song"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":20,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":30,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"summon nature's ally IX","details":"aquatic animals only"}]}],"strength":54,"dexterity":6,"constitution":30,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":18,"charisma":21,"baseatk":20,"cmb":50,"cmd":58,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Augment Summoning","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Swim)"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (any one)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":27},{"skill":"Stealth","value":5},{"skill":"Swim","value":59}],"languages":["Aquan"],"sq":[{"type":"hold breath"}],"environments":["any oceans"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This is a tremendous sea creature, resembling a whale of gigantic proportions. Its humped back stands like a mountain, and its massive eye is nearly as large as a sailing ship. Its cavernous blowhole spews forth a jet of water like a cyclone.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Smashing Breach","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action, a leviathan can make a special charge attack against creatures on the surface of the water. At the end of its charge, the leviathan breaches, then slams down onto the target with incredible force. Any Huge or smaller creatures in the leviathan's space must make a DC 30 Reflex save or take 4d8+33 points of bludgeoning damage and be forced into the nearest square that is adjacent to the whale. This breach automatically attempts to capsize any boats caught wholly or partially in this area. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Tail Storm","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action, a leviathan can raise its massive tail and bring it crashing down into the water, causing a massive wave that sinks ships in the area. The resulting wave fans out from the leviathan's tail in a 100-foot cone. Huge or smaller ships caught in the area and within 10 ft. of the leviathan's tail automatically sink. Creatures in the water and within 10 ft. of the leviathan's tail take 4d6+22 points bludgeoning damage. A successful DC 42 Reflex save reduces the damage by half. Additionally, a creature that fails its save is pushed 6d6 x 10 ft. away. Huge or smaller ships more than 10 ft. away within the area must succeed on a Profession (sailor) check or capsize. The DC of this check is 42, decreasing by 5 for every 10 ft. from the leviathan a ship is. The DC increases by a cumulative +5 for each size smaller than Huge a ship is. The save and base check DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Whale Song","kind":"Su","details":"As a swift action, a leviathan can unleash a song that is so deep and of such low frequency that the vibrations alone have adverse effects on living creatures. Any living creature within 100 ft. of a singing leviathan must succeed on a DC 30 Fortitude save or be stunned for 1d6 rounds. A creature that succeeds on its save is unaffected by that leviathan's whale song for one day. This song is more felt than heard, and can be detected by creatures up to 10 miles away. Creatures capable of detecting extremely low-frequency sounds (e.g. dolphins, whales, other leviathans) can detect this song up to 100 miles away. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Legend holds that there is but one leviathan in every ocean in the world, each creature being the undisputed sovereign of its domain. Smaller leviathans control the seas, whilst the tiniest-still massive by any measure-lurk in a few secluded bays within the lonelier parts of the world. Completely unopposed by any other creature, they dominate their realms. When a leviathan grows to such size that it can no longer be supported by its territory, it challenges another larger in size, seeking to gain mastery of its sea or ocean. Failure in this challenge results in death but if it overcomes its rival, the leviathan assumes sovereignty of the domain. Battles between these titanic creatures are an awesome sight to behold, for tidal waves and hurricanes erupt, devastating nearby coastal settlements.\n\nLeviathans are over 500 ft. long and weigh many hundreds of tons.\n\nLeviathans are seldom stirred to anger and only attack to defend themselves from opponents who can truly harm them-a rare occurrence indeed. They strike with their massive tail or by biting. A leviathan is so immense that it cannot bite any creature smaller than Huge; such small prey is simply swallowed whole. Any enemy flanking a leviathan from behind is attacked with a devastating tail slap or subjected to the leviathan's tail storm attack.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Amalgamation","cr":20,"xp":307200,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"construct","init":9,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"100 ft."},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":25,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+10 deflection, +9 Dex, -4 size","hp":225,"hd":"30d10+60","hdvalue":30,"fort":10,"ref":19,"will":15,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["construct traits (+60 hp)","magic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"varies +33 (damage by weapon)","ranged":"varies +35 (damage by weapon)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"multiple attacks"},{"type":"swarm attack","details":"10d6"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":28,"wisdom":20,"charisma":1,"baseatk":30,"cmb":41,"cmd":60,"sq":[{"type":"item use"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard (varies with individual Amalgamation)","description_visual":"A large collection of items rises up, forming into a swirling chaos that is the body of this being. The items move about throughout its bulk, somehow not touching one another in their mad dance.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Item Use","kind":"Su","details":"The amalgamation can use any of the items contained within its bulk. When activating magic items, it is considered to be using them as if a person of the required class, with a 20 in any relevant ability scores (or its natural scores, whichever are better). Furthermore, because of its innate magical nature, the save DC against any effects produced by magic items is 2 greater than normal. Finally, it can wield weapons and items as if it were of the appropriate size class for their type, so it suffers no hit penalties for being a Gargantuan construct with such items. Unless instructed otherwise, the amalgamation uses items at random from its bulk. However, it doesn't target them randomly-it uses them with care and precision, as if it had 18 Intelligence. Items with limited uses, such as scrolls and wands, are expended normally."},{"type":"Multiple Attacks","kind":"Ex","details":"The amalgamation can activate and use up to five items per round. It can therefore attack with weapons, activate magic items, hurl alchemical items like thunderstones, or slam random objects against opponents."},{"type":"Swarm Attack","kind":"Ex","details":"The amalgamation can move over enemies and damage them with the flying weapons and objects composing its bulk. It does this simply by moving over its victims, who are allowed either a DC 34 Reflex save or an attack of opportunity against the amalgamation, at their option. Anyone who begins their turn engulfed by the amalgamation takes 10d6 points of damage per round, with a DC 34 Reflex save allowed for half. This isn't considered an area effect for the purposes of evasion and similar abilities. The damage inflicted by the amalgamation overcomes all forms of damage reduction except epic. The save DC for both Reflex saves is Dexterity-based. Further, this damage is considered continuous for the purposes of determining if it disrupts spellcasting, concentration and the like."},{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"The amalgamation is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted: Dispel magic and greater dispel magic can be used to deactivate magic items, as per a targeted item dispel. Mage's disjunction causes it to subside into quiescence for 1d4+1 rounds, during which time it is considered helpless."}],"description":"The amalgamation is a special creation used by certain ancient spellcasters to defend their hordes and treasure vaults-for even should the guardian fall, most of the items being guarded would be destroyed, and hence not fall into enemy hands. The creature is composed of a large number of magical and mundane items, and it can use any of them to attack. Because of its magical nature, the amalgamation can even wield magic items such as wands without penalty. The amalgamation resembles a vortex or cloud of items 20 ft. in diameter, swirling within a shimmering field of energy. The precise appearance of the construct depends on the items that comprise its bulk.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"}];
